Two important key files of GOLANG are go.mod file and go.sum file. The go.mod file explicityly lists all direct and indirect dependencies required by GO project along with their precise versions. While the go.sum file stores the cryptographic checksums or hashes to verify if each of the dependency listed in go.mod file are not corrupted. GO verifies the downloaded modules if they match the recorded checksums present in the go.sum file. If both of them doesn't match it indicated that the dependency has been corrupted, as a consequence the build project will be failed. So to import other packages or build the package we need go.mod file and to ensure its not corrupted we need go.sum file.

