There are three different keywords in Go that are used for error handling. These are defer, panic and recover. The defer keyword is used when we want to do something at the end of the execution of the function in which defer statement is written. Either when all the statements are executed or some error occured and execution of the function has stopped, irrespective these situations the defer statements will be executed. All these defer statements are executed in the LIFO order. For example we would like to close the opened files in the function itself, however due to some error the entire function is not executed then file might not be closed, so if  we close it using the defer even if some panic occurs the file will be closed. We use panic keyword when we found an error in the code that leads to an error, it is like raising an issue and stopping the flow of executoion of the remaining part of the function. The recover function is used inside the defer function to handle the cases of the panic. This way we can handle the unexpected errors in program.

